manoid in appearance, upon arrival on Earth they take on the appearances of a rabbit (Bokko), a horse (Nokko), and a duck (Pukko) that they had captured as examples of Earth life forms. While on Earth they travel in a tire-shaped vehicle capable of enormous speeds called the Big Wheel, which can travel on both land and water (and, with modifications, through the air).\n\nThe series tackles a number of issues which were surprisingly progressive for an animated cartoon of that period; particularly ecological concerns and poverty."},"tags":[{"name":"Achromatic","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Animals","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Shounen","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Environmental","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Space","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Espionage","rank":20,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"The Amazing 3","english":"The Amazing 3","native":"ワンダースリー","romaji":"Wonder 3","synonyms":[{"language":"ja","source":"bangumi","value":"W3"},{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"三神奇"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"The Wonder 3"},{"language":null,"source":"bangumi","value":"W3(ワンダースリー)"}]},"trailer":{"id":"c7snhrdjhn8","site":"youtube","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/c7snhrdjhn8/hqdefault.jpg"},"visibility":"general"}